{
  "info": {
    "title": "Ozone Connect - Bank Data Sharing APIs",
    "contact": {
      "name": "Ozone Financial Technology Limited"
    },
    "description": "This document provides an API description in [OpenAPI](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.0.1.html)\nfor Bank Data Sharing APIs for Ozone Connect.\n\nThese APIs should be implemented by an financial institution so that Ozone\ncan expose these end-points to TPPs.\n\n#### Implementer Notes\n\nImplementers should note that this API prescribes a positive response for correctly executed\noperations including those where no data is returned. This is consistent with the general principles\nof REST.\nFor example, if the operation \n`get /accounts/{accountId}/products` is invoked and no product data is found for the account\nassociated with the value of `accountId` then the correct response is to return a `200` and an empty\narray: `{ \"data\": [] }`.\n\nPlease refer to the API Hub documentation for details of test cases that are \navailable for this API using the Ozone Connect test suite.\n\n### Versioning\n\nThe `version` property implements the following pattern `{standards-major}.{standards-minor}.{ozone-connect-version}`, where:\n\n* `standards-major` is the major version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n* `standards-minor` is the minor version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n* `ozone-connect-version` is the version of the Ozone Connect API description.\n\nSo, for example, `v2.0.1` indicates the first version of the Ozone Connect API description that implements the UAE standard version 2.0.\n**Please adhere to the deprecated flags in your implementation. Do not implement deprecated properties when** **implementing new functionality.**\n\n### v2.2.3\n* Changed `emiratesId` on `CustomerPersonClaims` to carry\n  `pattern: ^784-?[0-9]{4}-?[0-9]{7}-?[0-9]{1}$`, so the Emirates ID returned by `get /customer` and\n  `get /accounts/{accountId}/customer` is well-formed. This is the pattern already used by the Insurance API\n  description and, from v2.2, by `post /leads` in the Bank Products Data API description. Per OFP-009.\n\n* Changed `fullName`, `givenName`, `familyName`, `middleName` and `nickname` on `CustomerPersonClaims` to accept\n  Latin letters, space, apostrophe, period and hyphen only, and `businessName` on `CustomerCorporateClaims` to\n  accept those plus digits, ampersand, comma, parentheses and forward slash. Field lengths are unchanged.\n  Per OFP-009.\n\n### v2.2.2\n* Changed `transactionInformation` on `CbuaeTransaction` to be required, so every transaction returned by\n  `get /accounts/{accountId}/transactions` carries a narrative by which the customer can recognise the entry.\n  The field also gains `minLength: 1` and `maxLength: 500`, matching the bounds the TPP-facing\n  `TransactionInformation` schema has carried since v2.1. The same requirement is applied to `AETransaction` in\n  the Standards Account Information API description, since the API Hub can only return a narrative the LFI\n  supplied.\n\n* Changed the `post /customers/action/cop-query` request to carry the account IBAN only. `data.account.name` is\n  removed, along with the `PersonName` and `BusinessName` Schema Objects it referenced. The LFI performs no\n  matching, so the name submitted by the TPP is no longer sent to it.\n\n* Changed the `post /customers/action/cop-query` response to carry the account holder's name directly. Each\n  entry in `data` is now an `id` and a `name`, which is either a `CbuaeCopPersonName` (`fullName` required) or a\n  `CbuaeCopBusinessName` (`businessName` required). The `verifiedClaims` / `verification` identity-assurance\n  envelope is removed from this operation, along with the `CbuaeVerifiedCopClaim` and\n  `ConfirmationOfPayeePersonClaims` Schema Objects and the wider customer data the latter carried — none of it\n  is needed to compare two names, and Confirmation of Payee runs without a consent. `number` is dropped for the\n  same reason; `id` is retained as the handle for investigating a disputed result. Structured name fields\n  (`firstName`, `middleName`, `lastName`, `fullNameAr`, `alsoKnownAs`, `businessNameAr`) are retained as\n  optional members so the matching algorithm can be improved without a further change to this contract.\n  `get /accounts/{accountId}/customer` is unaffected: it has its own `CbuaeCustomer` / `CbuaeVerifiedClaim`\n  Schema Objects.\n\n### v2.2.1\n* Added new version compatible with v2.2 of standards.\n* Changed `get /accounts/{accountId}/products` to return `ExpectedProfitRates`, providing one-or-more deposit\n  rates for Sharia-compliant products. Each rate carries `RateType` (`FixedProfit` or `VariableProfit`),\n  `DepositRateType` (`ExpectedProfitRate` or `IndicativeProfitRate`), `ProfitSharingRatio`,\n  `ProfitDistributionMethod`, `ProfitDistributionFrequency`, an optional `Description`, and `RateDetails`.\n\n* Changed `get /accounts/{accountId}/products` to return `ShariaFinanceRates`, providing one-or-more finance\n  rates for Sharia-compliant products. As with `FinanceRates`, this can be provided in cleartext or as a JWE\n  based on the preference of the LFI for sharing this information. Each cleartext rate is discriminated on\n  `RateType` as a fixed profit rate, a variable profit rate or a hybrid profit rate, and carries\n  `ProfitCalculationMethod` with the values `PrincipalBalance`, `OutstandingBalance`,\n  `InitialDrawdownAmount`, `UnusedCreditLine` or `UtilizedLimit`.\n\n* Changed `get /accounts/{accountId}/products` to return `TakafulRequired`, indicating whether Takaful\n  coverage is required for the product, and `TakafulDescription`, describing the type and purpose of the\n  required coverage.\n\n* Changed `get /accounts/{accountId}/products` to return `ProfitCalculationMethod` on charge components, for\n  use in place of `InterestCalculationMethod` where the product uses Islamic calculation methods.\n\n* Changed `InterestCalculationMethod` on charge components returned by\n  `get /accounts/{accountId}/products` to apply to interest only. Islamic calculation methods are now\n  described by `ProfitCalculationMethod`.\n\n* Changed `RateDetails` on the deposit rates returned by `get /accounts/{accountId}/products` to reference a\n  shared Schema Object, so that the same rate structure is used by both `DepositRates` and\n  `ExpectedProfitRates`. No change to the properties returned.\n\n* Changed `get /accounts/{accountId}/balances`, `get /accounts/{accountId}/transactions` and\n  `get /accounts/{accountId}/statements` to return `BalanceDescription`, allowing a description of the\n  balance to be provided identifying the specific Shari'ah compliant charges, payments and rewards made\n  which can affect the balance.\n",
    "version": "v2.2.3"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://[Ozone_Connect_API]"
    }
  ],
  "source_path": "/accounts/{accountId}/balances",
  "operations": {
    "get": {
      "tags": [
        "balances"
      ],
      "summary": "Fetch the balances for the account specified by the account id.",
      "operationId": "findBalancesByAccountId",
      "description": "The financial institution may return more than one balance record for each account. Each array element represents a balance of a different type, mapped to a specific ISO 20022 code.",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/providerId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/aspspId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerOrgId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerClientId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerSoftwareStatementId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/apiUri"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/apiOperation"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/consentId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerInteractionId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ozoneInteractionId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/psuIdentifier"
        },
        {
          "name": "accountId",
          "in": "path",
          "description": "Id of the account to be queried",
          "required": true,
          "schema": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/page"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/page-size"
        }
      ],
      "responses": {
        "200": {
          "description": "successful operation",
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BalancesResponse"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "400": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequestError"
        },
        "401": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/UnauthorizedError"
        },
        "403": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/ForbiddenError"
        },
        "500": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/InternalServerError"
        },
        "default": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/Error"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "security": [
    {},
    {
      "OzoneConnectApiKey": []
    },
    {
      "OzoneConnectClientCredentials": [
        "placeholder"
      ]
    },
    {
      "OzoneConnectJwtAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "securitySchemes": {
    "OzoneConnectApiKey": {
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using an API Key, which is a secret shared between the API Hub and the LFI.",
      "type": "apiKey",
      "in": "header",
      "name": "Authorization"
    },
    "OzoneConnectClientCredentials": {
      "type": "oauth2",
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using a Client Credentials grant type.\n\nLFIs must host an OAuth 2.0 Authorization Server to utilise this security pattern. Scope values are set during the onboarding process, and represented by a placeholder in this API description.\n",
      "flows": {
        "clientCredentials": {
          "tokenUrl": "https://example.lfi.ae/token",
          "scopes": {
            "placeholder": "Placeholder for scopes, which are set by the LFI during onboarding"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "OzoneConnectJwtAuth": {
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using the \"JWT Auth\" mechanism, where the Client presents a signed JSON Web Token as a credential.\n\nThe Server MUST verify the signature in order to authenticate the Client.\n\nPlease note that the value of the `scheme` parameter is not a registered HTTP Authentication Scheme, to indicate it is specific to Ozone Connect. Please refer to API Hub documentation for further details.\n",
      "type": "http",
      "scheme": "Ozone-Connect-JWT-Auth"
    }
  }
}

